<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    THE GENETIC ARCHIVE (spec §5b) — "vanilla Biotech GeneDefs framed as 'what
    has wandered in over the centuries', curated under the P-laws, replaceable
    by the campaign/any mod (§9)."

    🔑 THIS IS A DEF, NOT A LIST IN CODE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. The RUT
    layer swaps the campaign's frozen SW gene lists in by shipping its own
    RM_GeneArchiveDef with a HIGHER `priority`; Dialog_GeneArchive reads
    whichever archive wins. Nothing in this mod's C# names a single gene.

    ⚠️ OPEN QUESTION 1 (spec §10): "Default archive size for the universal
    list: ~12-20 vanilla/Biotech genes under the P-laws proposed [INVENTED] —
    curate at a sitting or delegate to build?" This is the BUILD's curation,
    17 targets and 19 riders, offered for the owner's sitting. Every defName
    below was read out of the live GeneDef index (RimSage), not guessed.

    THE P-LAWS, and how this list obeys them:

    P4 — EVERY GENE IS A TRADE, never pure upside. The targets are genuinely
      good; the price is not paid in the target, it is paid in the RIDER, the
      coma, the antidote, the walk, and the Slime-marked penalty. A target
      list of gifts with a guaranteed cost attached IS the anti-exponential
      rule; a target list of gifts with no cost would not be.
    P5 — RIDERS ARE VISIBLE AND FELT. Every rider below is one or the other
      and most are both: a mood floor, a melee penalty, a fragility, or a
      body change other pawns can see. NOTHING in the rider list is cosmetic-
      only-and-harmless, and nothing in it is invisible-and-harmless.
    P7 — the Slime-marked social penalty is applied per injection by
      CompTargetEffect_InjectSlimeGenes, not listed here.
    P8 — HERITABLE. The injector adds these as ENDOGENES
      (Pawn_GeneTracker.AddGene(def, xenogene: false)), so the bloodline
      carries them. That is in the C#, not here.

    🔴 ONE EXCLUSION THAT IS A RULING, NOT A TASTE: no Aggression_Aggressive
    or Aggression_HyperAggressive, anywhere, in either list. The never-hostile
    law (§3 law 2) is about slimification, but the library filing a colonist
    as "more likely to attack people" is the same ruling read one step out,
    and a future editor should have to argue with this comment first.
  -->

  <RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.GeneArchiveDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">
    <defName>RM_Archive_Default</defName>
    <label>the circulating archive</label>
    <description>Everything that ever touched the body, still in circulation.</description>
    <priority>0</priority>

    <!-- What a player can ASK FOR. 17 entries: 16 vanilla, plus the one this
         mod authors, which is the only way off the ladder short of leaving. -->
    <targetGenes>
      <li>RM_Gene_SlimeResistance</li>
      <li>ToxResist_Total</li>
      <li>ToxicEnvironmentResistance_Total</li>
      <li>FireResistant</li>
      <li>VacuumResistance_Partial</li>
      <li>MoveSpeed_VeryQuick</li>
      <li>Beauty_Beautiful</li>
      <li>Learning_Fast</li>
      <li>Mood_Sanguine</li>
      <li>Pain_Reduced</li>
      <li>MeleeDamage_Strong</li>
      <li>MinTemp_LargeDecrease</li>
      <li>MaxTemp_LargeIncrease</li>
      <li>PsychicAbility_Enhanced</li>
      <li>Coagulate</li>
      <li>AcidSpray</li>
      <li>FoamSpray</li>
    </targetGenes>

    <!-- What comes WITH it, one rolled per injection, unseen until it lands.
         "Something fun but odd" (ruled) — but always felt. -->
    <riderGenes>
      <li>Beauty_VeryUgly</li>
      <li>Beauty_Ugly</li>
      <li>Mood_Pessimist</li>
      <li>Mood_Depressive</li>
      <li>Pain_Extra</li>
      <li>Learning_Slow</li>
      <li>Delicate</li>
      <li>MeleeDamage_Weak</li>
      <li>MinTemp_SmallIncrease</li>
      <li>MaxTemp_SmallDecrease</li>
      <li>PsychicAbility_Dull</li>
      <li>Aggression_DeadCalm</li>
      <li>Hair_LightGreen</li>
      <li>Skin_PaleYellow</li>
      <li>Ears_Floppy</li>
      <li>Tail_Smooth</li>
      <li>ElongatedFingers</li>
      <li>Brow_Heavy</li>
      <li>Head_Gaunt</li>
    </riderGenes>
  </RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.GeneArchiveDef>

</Defs>
